{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/2/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d255d7a7\" lines=\"99-114\">\n<description>\nMove the patterned edge band to the opposite edge along every row or column whose band slice contains the trail color.\n\nInput structure\n- The dominant color is the background.\n- The two foreground colors are a frequent trail color and a rarer marker color.\n- All marker pixels lie nearest to one grid edge, and that edge contains trail-color runs that define the source-band thickness.\n\nRule\n- Choose the source edge identified by the marker pixels.\n- A row or column perpendicular to that edge moves if its source-band slice contains the trail color.\n- Copy that slice unchanged to the opposite edge, erase the remaining trail cells to background, and keep marker-only lines fixed.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker color identifies the active edge, while the trail color identifies which parallel rows or columns carry an edge-band slice across the grid.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a32d8b75\" lines=\"262-275\">\n<description>\nAssemble and place enlarged sprites on a canvas using legend-panel instructions.\n\nInput structure:\n- Color-6 separators divide the grid into a left legend column and a main canvas.\n- Each legend panel has (top to bottom): a unit sprite, a frame template, a 5x5 bordered square with a position-marker pixel, and a 3x3 rotation clock-hand.\n\nRule:\n- Tile the unit sprite into each active cell of the frame to build an enlarged composite.\n- Rotate the composite per the clock-hand direction (up=0, right=90, down=180, left=270 degrees).\n- Place it on the canvas anchored at the position encoded by the marker pixel's row/col in the bordered square's 3x3 inner grid.\n\nKey insight: The marker pixel's position in a 3x3 grid jointly encodes vertical and horizontal anchor alignment (start/middle/end).\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"13f06aa5\" lines=\"36-51\">\n<description>\nExtend each colored marker from its directional sprite to a grid edge, painting a dotted ray and the whole edge side.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- One repeated body color forms small 8-connected directional sprites.\n- Each marker is a singleton non-background, non-body color embedded in one sprite.\n\nRule:\n- The body pixels around a marker lie mostly behind it; the opposite direction is the marker's ray direction.\n- Paint every second pixel from the marker along that ray, then paint the entire boundary side reached by the ray.\n- If two painted boundary sides meet at a corner, make that shared corner black.\n\nKey insight:\n- The same seven-pixel body sprite rotates to encode the direction; its local center-of-mass bias points away from the ray.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"4df5b0ae\" lines=\"27-41\">\n<description>\nPack the colored sprites along the bottom edge from smallest to largest.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background color and several monochrome 4-connected\nforeground sprites; a full-grid one-cell frame may surround the scene.\n\nRule\nRemove any full-grid rectangular frame, sort the remaining sprites by pixel\narea from smallest to largest, and paste their bounding-box sprites left to\nright with each sprite bottom-aligned.\n\nKey insight\nThe original locations do not determine the final slots; each sprite's area\ngives the packing order, while its shape and color are preserved.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d749d46f\" lines=\"32-51\">\n<description>\nPack each solid foreground rectangle twice: wide across the top and tall from the bottom.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has one background color and one foreground color; the foreground forms\nseparate solid rectangles, ordered from left to right.\n\nRule\nBuild a 10-row background canvas whose width is the packed width of the wide\nversions of the rectangles. For each source rectangle, paint a top-aligned\nrectangle of shape min(h,w) by max(h,w), with one background column between\nconsecutive rectangles. Then, starting again from the left edge, paint a\nbottom-aligned rectangle of shape max(h,w) by min(h,w) for each source rectangle,\nagain separated by one background column.\n\nKey insight\nThe input rectangles are not copied in their original orientations; each object\ncontributes one horizontal-facing and one vertical-facing normalized rectangle,\npreserving left-to-right object order.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"271d71e2\" lines=\"9-22\">\n<description>\nMove bordered containers toward same-colored destination markers, charging gray cells to orange.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = 6 (magenta). Black-bordered (0) rectangles with gray (5) / orange (7) interiors.\n- A head sprite (9) sits adjacent to one container edge; a matching destination sprite lies along the movement axis.\n\nRule:\n- Each container translates toward its destination along the head-to-dest axis.\n- Steps = min(head-to-dest distance, number of gray interior cells).\n- Gray cells become orange from the head-facing side inward, one per step.\n\nKey insight: Gray cell count caps movement — a container stops short if it runs out of gray cells to charge.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"bae5c565\" lines=\"10-28\">\n<description>\nErase the top palette row and redraw it below as a widening wedge centered on its missing cell.\n\nInput structure\n- The top row is a palette row with exactly one background gap.\n- Below it, the only foreground is one vertical marker bar of a single color.\n- The marker bar is either in the gap column or immediately beside it.\n\nRule\n- Clear the grid to background.\n- Starting at the top of the marker bar, each next row copies one more\n  column of the top-row palette on both sides of the gap.\n- Fill the gap column with the marker color, and keep the vertical marker bar.\n\nKey insight\n- The lone background cell in the top row is the center of the expanding\n  copy; the lower vertical bar provides the center color and the row where\n  the expansion begins.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"d59b0160\" lines=\"39-54\">\n<description>\nDelete connected components whose colors match a legend swatch.\n\nInput structure:\n- Background (bg) fills most of the grid.\n- Top-left corner: a small square legend region bordered on its bottom and right edges by a single color; the interior holds a set of \"target\" colors.\n- Elsewhere: multicolored objects (4-connected components) on the bg.\n\nRule:\n- Read the target color set from inside the legend border.\n- For each connected component, check whether it contains **all** target colors.\n- Erase (fill with bg) every component that does; leave all others unchanged.\n- Output grid is the same size.\n\nKey insight: The legend acts as a filter specification — only components carrying the full color palette shown in the legend are removed.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"53fb4810\" lines=\"105-119\">\n<description>\nExtend marker tiles outward from '+' shapes by repeating them to the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- A dominant non-bg color forms several '+'-shaped objects.\n- Small colored patches (1–few cells) sit adjacent to each arm of a '+'.\n\nRule:\n- For each marker tile touching a '+', determine which side of the '+' it sits on.\n- Project the tile away from the '+' in that direction, repeating the tile pattern periodically until the grid boundary.\n- '+' pixels are never overwritten.\n\nKey insight: Each marker's attachment side determines its extension direction; the pattern repeats periodically, not as a single copy.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6ca952ad\" lines=\"15-30\">\n<description>\nDrop every large foreground object straight down to the bottom while leaving small marker objects fixed.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a dominant background color and exactly one foreground color.\n- The foreground is split into separated 4-connected objects.\n- Objects of area at most three are stationary markers; larger objects are moving sprites.\n\nRule:\n- Clear each moving sprite from its original position.\n- Translate each moving sprite vertically downward until its bbox bottom reaches the grid bottom.\n- Repaint each translated sprite in its original color; small markers stay unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- Object area separates the active falling sprites from the small fixed markers, and all active sprites follow the same vertical path.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"21897d95\" lines=\"283-301\">\n<description>\nRepaint regions from T-shaped control markers, erase the markers, and optionally rotate based on a color-9 L-marker.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is a mosaic of monochrome regions.\n- Color 1 forms T-shaped control markers on region boundaries.\n- Some controls use three singleton color-1 pixels around a colored center; that center is a literal replacement color.\n- An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker triggers 90-degree rotation of the output.\n\nRule:\n- For a color-1 T marker, the single stem points at the destination region to repaint.\n- The two diagonal cells behind the stem identify the source region; the destination gets that source region's original color.\n- For a colored-center T marker, the same stem identifies the destination, but the center color is the replacement.\n- All marker cells are filled with the final color of the source-side region.\n- A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) → CCW 90°, ┌ (corner top-left) → CW 90°.\n\nKey insight:\n- The stem chooses what changes, while the two diagonals behind the stem choose where the marker itself belongs.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"a416fc5b\" lines=\"95-106\">\n<description>\nAdd the two missing colored arms of a centered diamond-sprite motif, or clear a completed motif to a blank square.\n\nInput structure\nAn 11x11 board has orange background and pink separator bars forming nine 3x3 cells. Occupied cells contain a four-pixel diamond sprite; the center cell and one neighboring cell are red, and a completed board may also contain one grey and one teal sprite.\n\nRule\nWith only the two red sprites present, preserve the board and add grey and teal diamond sprites 135 degrees clockwise and counterclockwise from the non-center red arm. If those expected grey and teal sprites are already present, output an all-background square whose side length is the total number of sprite pixels.\n\nKey insight\nThe non-center red sprite is an eight-neighbor direction from the center; the other two colored arms are fixed rotations of that direction.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"538b439f\" lines=\"122-142\">\n<description>\nReflect the solid rectangular source objects across the full separator line and color the gap with the separator color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background contains one full-width or full-height one-pixel\n  separator line in a non-background color.\n- One other foreground color forms solid rectangular objects, all strictly on the same side of that separator.\n- Remaining non-background pixels are scattered distractors.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the input grid shape and unchanged pixels outside each affected corridor.\n- Mirror each source object across the separator line.\n- For every source object, recolor the rectangular strip between the\n  original object and its reflection to the separator color, then paint the\n  reflected object in the source color.\n\nKey insight:\n- The full straight line is a mirror axis; the real objects are identified\n  structurally as the only solid rectangles confined to one side, while\n  scattered pixels are noise that may be overwritten inside the corridor.\n</description>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/2/des.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/2/des.md\"","aggregated_output":"<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据封闭区域内部的孔洞数量，从颜色图例中选取对应颜色重新填充该区域的轮廓。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（如 Black）。\n  - 网格左侧有一列纵向排列的小正方形颜色图例块（从上到下依次为不同颜色，如 Red、Blue、Green、Yellow 等），每个图例块为 2x2 纯色方块，图例块之间间隔一行背景色。\n  - 网格右侧有若干用 Grey 像素绘制的不规则封闭区域（4-连通闭合轮廓），每个区域内部填充背景色，但区域内部散布着若干 Maroon 色的单像素点（代表\"孔洞\"）。\n  - 每个封闭区域内的孔洞数量各不相同，范围在 1 到图例块总数之间。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 数出每个 Grey 封闭区域内部 Maroon 孔洞像素的数量 N。\n  - 从左侧颜色图例中，取第 N 个图例块的颜色（从上到下第 1 个图例对应 N=1）。\n  - 将该封闭区域的 Grey 轮廓像素全部重绘为该图例颜色，同时擦除区域内部的 Maroon 孔洞像素（变为背景色）。\n  - 左侧颜色图例保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：孔洞的数量不是装饰——它是查表索引，将每个封闭区域映射到图例中的特定颜色。解题者需要先发现\"数孔洞\"这一隐含步骤，再发现孔洞计数与图例位置的对应关系。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：识别每个彩色对象的对称性类型，根据对称性类型决定该对象的变换方式并从底部标记条中查找目标颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（如 Azure）。\n  - 网格中散布着若干互不重叠的小型彩色精灵（sprite），每个精灵由单一非背景颜色构成，面积在 4-8 像素之间。\n  - 每个精灵恰好具有以下三种对称性之一：（a）仅关于水平中轴对称（上下对称但左右不对称），（b）仅关于垂直中轴对称（左右对称但上下不对称），（c）180 度旋转对称（但不具有任何轴对称性）。\n  - 网格底部有一行三个 2x2 的颜色标记块，从左到右分别对应三种对称性类型，顺序固定为：第一个对应水平对称类、第二个对应垂直对称类、第三个对应旋转对称类。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 判断每个精灵的对称性类型。\n  - 仅水平对称的精灵：将其在原位上下翻转（沿水平轴镜像），颜色替换为底部标记中第一个色块的颜色。\n  - 仅垂直对称的精灵：形状不变（左右翻转后与原形状相同），但颜色替换为底部标记中第二个色块的颜色。\n  - 180 度旋转对称的精灵：形状位置不变，颜色替换为底部标记中第三个色块的颜色。\n  - 底部标记行在输出中被擦除为背景色。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者必须首先识别每个精灵的对称性类别（这需要逐一检查形状的对称轴和旋转不变性），然后发现底部的颜色条是按对称性类别排列的颜色映射表。对称性的判定和颜色查表构成两层独立的推理。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将散落的碎片拼回到模板形状的缺口中，碎片的颜色决定其所属模板，碎片需要旋转至正确朝向才能严丝合缝地填入缺口。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（如 Black）。\n  - 网格中有若干个大型矩形区域，每个矩形区域用不同颜色填充（如 Red、Blue、Green），但每个矩形区域内有一块连通的缺口（缺口处为背景色），缺口形状不规则但面积较小（3-6 像素）。\n  - 网格中另有若干散落的小型碎片精灵，每个碎片的颜色与某个矩形区域的颜色相同，面积恰好与该矩形区域的缺口面积相等。\n  - 碎片的原始朝向可能需要旋转 0°、90°、180° 或 270° 才能恰好与对应缺口的形状吻合。每个碎片只有唯一一种旋转角度能与目标缺口完全匹配。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 根据颜色将每个碎片与对应的矩形区域配对。\n  - 将碎片尝试四种旋转（0°、90°、180°、270°），找到能与缺口形状完全吻合的唯一旋转角度。\n  - 将旋转后的碎片填入缺口位置，使矩形区域变为完整的实心矩形。\n  - 碎片的原始位置在输出中被擦除为背景色。\n\n- `Key insight`：颜色匹配是第一层推理（碎片属于哪个矩形），旋转拼合是第二层推理（碎片需要旋转多少度才能填入缺口）。解题者不能仅靠颜色配对——还必须在四种旋转中找到唯一能吻合缺口轮廓的那一种。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：利用分隔线将网格划分为多个子区域，在每个子区域中找到唯一与其他精灵形状不同的\"异类对象\"，然后将所有异类对象按阅读顺序拼成紧凑的输出网格。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 网格被 Magenta 色的完整直线（横线和竖线）分割成若干大小相等的矩形子区域（例如形成 2x3 或 3x2 的子区域阵列）。\n  - 每个子区域的背景为主色（如 Black），内部有若干用同一种非背景颜色绘制的小型精灵对象（每个精灵为 4-连通的像素块，面积 3-6 像素）。\n  - 在每个子区域中，大部分精灵在形状上完全相同（例如都是某种 L 形），但恰好有一个精灵的形状与同区域内其他精灵不同——这就是该区域的\"异类\"。\n  - 不同子区域中异类精灵的形状和颜色各不相同。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 在每个子区域内，通过比较所有精灵的形状（将每个精灵平移至原点后比对像素图案），找出形状只出现一次的那个精灵。\n  - 将该异类精灵裁剪为其最小包围盒。\n  - 按子区域的阅读顺序（从左到右、从上到下），将所有异类精灵的包围盒排列到一个新的输出网格中：输出网格的列数等于子区域的列数，行数等于子区域的行数；每个位置放置对应子区域的异类精灵包围盒，各包围盒之间用一列/一行背景色分隔。\n  - Magenta 分隔线不出现在输出中。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要两步推理——首先在每个子区域中完成\"找不同\"任务（比对形状而非颜色，因为同区域内颜色相同），然后理解异类对象按子区域空间位置的阅读顺序重排进紧凑网格的排列规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据嵌套同心矩形框的层数决定最内层图案的旋转角度，层数越深旋转幅度越大。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（如 Black）。\n  - 网格中有若干组独立的嵌套同心矩形框结构，各组之间互不重叠。每组由若干层空心矩形边框构成，从外到内每一层使用不同颜色（如最外层 Red、次外层 Blue、最内层 Green 等），相邻两层之间间隔一像素宽的背景色。\n  - 每组的最内层矩形框内部包含一个用 Yellow 色绘制的非对称小图案（如 L 形或 F 形，面积 3-5 像素），图案不具备任何旋转对称性。\n  - 不同组的嵌套框层数各不相同（范围 1-4 层）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 数出每组嵌套结构中矩形框的层数 N。\n  - 将该组最内层的 Yellow 图案在其所在区域的中心位置顺时针旋转 N×90 度（1 层旋转 90°，2 层旋转 180°，3 层旋转 270°，4 层旋转 360° 即恢复原样）。\n  - 旋转后的图案放回最内层框的中心位置，所有矩形框轮廓保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：矩形框的嵌套层数不是纯粹的装饰结构——每多一层框对应多 90 度的顺时针旋转。解题者需要先注意到不同组中内部图案的朝向不同，再将旋转角度差异与可数的嵌套层数建立关联。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：每个彩色矩形沿接触的导轨线滑动，滑动距离等于矩形内部标记点的数量，导轨线和标记点最终被擦除。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（如 Azure）。\n  - 网格中有若干用不同颜色绘制的实心矩形色块（如 Red、Green、Blue 等），彼此不重叠，面积在 4-12 像素之间。\n  - 网格中有若干条 Grey 色的单像素宽直线，每条直线水平或垂直贯穿整个网格。这些直线充当\"导轨\"。\n  - 每个矩形色块恰好有一条边与某条导轨直线紧邻（间距为零，矩形的该边像素与导轨像素在 4-连通方向上相邻）。\n  - 每个矩形色块内部散布着若干 Maroon 色的单像素标记点（在矩形主颜色像素中嵌入），数量在 1-5 之间。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 确定每个矩形与哪条导轨接触，以及接触的是矩形的哪一侧。\n  - 滑动轴向由导轨方向决定：水平导轨→左右滑动，垂直导轨→上下滑动。\n  - 滑动方向由接触侧决定：矩形位于导轨上方时向右滑动，位于导轨下方时向左滑动；矩形位于导轨左方时向下滑动，位于导轨右方时向上滑动。\n  - 滑动距离（以像素为单位）等于该矩形内部 Maroon 标记点的数量。\n  - 输出中：矩形移动到新位置，内部 Maroon 标记点被替换为矩形自身的颜色（变为纯色矩形），所有 Grey 导轨线被擦除为背景色。\n\n- `Key insight`：三层信息来源各不相同——导轨方向编码滑动轴向，矩形与导轨的相对位置编码滑动的正负方向，而隐藏在矩形内部的标记点数量编码滑动距离。解题者必须依次发现每一层编码机制。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中的箭头形标记作为\"投射器\"，沿箭头指向将对应的源图案周期性地平铺到目标框内部。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（如 Black）。\n  - 网格中有若干小型彩色图案块（面积在 2x2 至 3x3 包围盒内的非背景色 4-连通体），每个图案块使用独特的前景颜色。\n  - 每个图案块的某一侧紧邻一个由 Red 像素构成的箭头标记。箭头绘制方式：3 个像素排成一行或一列作为箭身，箭身的一端向垂直于箭身的方向偏移 1 像素处有 1 个像素作为箭尖，箭尖所指即为投射方向（上、下、左、右四方向之一）。箭身紧贴图案块的一侧边缘。\n  - 网格中另有若干由 Grey 像素绘制的空心矩形框（单像素宽轮廓），框内部填充背景色。每个目标框的大小不同。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 从每个图案块出发，沿其箭头指向方向做射线投射，命中的第一个 Grey 目标框即为该图案块的配对目标。\n  - 将图案块的包围盒内容从目标框内部的箭头入射侧开始，沿箭头方向周期性平铺，填满目标框内部区域。若最后一轮图案超出框边界则截断。\n  - Red 箭头标记在输出中擦除为背景色，Grey 目标框轮廓保持不变，原始图案块保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：箭头同时编码两层信息——它既指定了图案块与目标框之间的配对关系（通过射线投射命中），又指定了图案在目标框内从哪一侧开始平铺的方向。解题者需要先理解射线配对逻辑，再理解周期性平铺的填充规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在网格的彩色路径网络中，路径交叉点处的颜色混合规则决定了交叉点的输出颜色，而路径本身保留其原始颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（如 Black）。\n  - 网格中有若干条单像素宽的直线路径（水平或垂直），每条路径使用一种独特的非背景颜色（如 Red、Blue、Green 等），路径从网格的一个边缘延伸到另一个边缘。\n  - 某些路径会相互交叉（一条水平路径与一条垂直路径在某个像素处重叠）。在输入中，交叉点处的像素颜色为两条路径中 ID 较小（即在网格中更靠左上方首次出现）的那条路径的颜色。\n  - 网格的四个角落各有一个 2x2 的颜色参考块：左上角为 Red，右上角为 Blue，左下角为 Green，右下角为 Yellow。这些参考块指示了颜色优先级排序。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 读取四个角落的颜色参考块，确定颜色优先级顺序（左上角 = 最高优先级，按顺时针方向优先级递减：左上 > 右上 > 右下 > 左下）。\n  - 对于每个路径交叉点（水平路径与垂直路径相交处），将该像素的颜色设置为两条交叉路径中优先级更高的那条路径的颜色。\n  - 非交叉点的路径像素保留原始颜色不变。角落的参考块在输出中保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现交叉点的颜色发生了变化，再从角落的颜色参考块中推断出颜色优先级规则。角落参考块不是装饰——它们定义了颜色之间的覆盖优先级，这一关联需要通过多个交叉点的颜色变化来归纳。\n</new_puzzle>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
